 "comments": [
  {
   "address": 49664,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Thirty-six space-padded 40-byte rows name the game staff, music credits, developer, publisher and game title, ending with a prompt to press a key. The zero at $C7A0 terminates the text passed to the story renderer at $1924."
  },
  {
   "address": 57344,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Use A to select a seven-byte record at $EB5C: one accumulator increment and three little-endian pointers. Clear the three $24-byte channel state blocks, initialize their pointers and counters from the selected record, clear SID registers, and enable the channel update flags."
  },
  {
   "address": 57942,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Read a two-byte sequence-table base from the stream into indexed voice state, then select the first pointer in that table."
  },
  {
   "address": 57958,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Add the indexed voice's offset to its sequence-table base and advance the offset. If the selected two-byte pointer is zero, reset to the first table entry; load the selected pointer into the stream pointer and continue reading."
  },
  {
   "address": 58087,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Copy three bytes from the sound stream into indexed voice state at $E0DF-$E0E1, advance the stream pointer by three, set $E0E2 to one, and continue reading commands."
  },
  {
   "address": 58125,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Select $80 for the indexed voice's $E0E3 state, then continue reading commands. The following entry points select $40, $20 or $10 instead."
  },
  {
   "address": 58145,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Clear two indexed voice state bytes, take the next stream byte into $E0D9, advance the pointer and continue reading commands."
  },
  {
   "address": 58173,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Set bit $20 in the indexed voice's $E0C2 state, clear $E0C9 and $E0CA, and copy three stream bytes to $E0CE-$E0D0. The $E341 entry sets bit $04 instead. Both advance the pointer by three and continue reading."
  },
  {
   "address": 58224,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Copy two stream bytes to the indexed voice's $E0DC and $E0DB state, copy the second to $E0DD, advance the pointer by two, and set $E0DE to $40."
  },
  {
   "address": 58258,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Clear the indexed voice's $E0DE state and continue reading the stream."
  },
  {
   "address": 58265,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Set the low two bits of the indexed voice's $E0C2 state and continue reading the stream."
  },
  {
   "address": 58275,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Count down the indexed voice's delay. When it expires, read its byte stream: values below $80 set the next value and reload the delay, $80-$BF dispatch through the command table, and higher values change stream parameters before reading again. Save the advanced pointer when a value is accepted."
  },
  {
   "address": 58429,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "For the channel selected by X, read a byte from the stream addressed by $E0CB/$E0CC plus $E0CD. A byte with bit 7 set resets the stream offset to $FF and has that bit cleared. Add $E0D3, the global offset at $E464 and $E0E5; use the result to select a little-endian frequency from $E5C2. The continuation at $E464 applies the channel's optional frequency and pulse adjustments and stores the resulting SID values in its state block."
  },
  {
   "address": 58468,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Immediate operand of the ADC at $E463. Initialization clears it; a sound-stream command at $E2C7 replaces it. The same routine then adds the channel byte at $E0E5, looks up a two-byte frequency and applies enabled pitch and pulse-width adjustments before storing the channel's frequency at $E0D6/$E0D7 and pulse width at $E0D8/$E0D9."
  },
  {
   "address": 58818,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The first 82 little-endian values in the sound driver's frequency lookup. The driver doubles its index and reads a pair at $E46C and $E471; the sampled story, Broadway and outcome selections read within this portion. The table's full extent remains open."
  },
  {
   "address": 58819,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The high byte of the first frequency value; the little-endian pairs begin one byte earlier at $E5C2 and continue through $E665."
  },
  {
   "address": 58984,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Fourteen low bytes of pointers selected by a stream command at $E3EF; the corresponding high bytes start at $E676."
  },
  {
   "address": 58998,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Fourteen high bytes paired with the low bytes at $E668, read by the command at $E3F5. The pointed-to data is not yet classified."
  },
  {
   "address": 59012,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 0 contains $00. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59013,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 1 contains $00, $03, $07. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59016,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 2 contains $00, $04, $07. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59019,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 3 contains $0C, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00, $00. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59027,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 4 contains $00, $04, $07, $0C. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59031,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 5 contains $07, $0C, $0F. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59034,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 6 contains $07, $0C, $10. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59037,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 7 contains $03, $07, $0C. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59040,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 8 contains $04, $07, $0C. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59043,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 9 contains $00, $0C. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59045,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 10 contains $00, $03. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59047,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 11 contains $00, $04. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59049,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 12 contains $00, $05. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59051,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Offset sequence 13 contains $00, $07. At $E43D the driver reads an offset, resets the sequence index when its high bit is set, masks that bit and adds the value to the voice state. The final byte here has its high bit set."
  },
  {
   "address": 59703,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Update the shared modulation state, then call each active voice's effect routine according to the three flags at $E12F-$E131."
  },
  {
   "address": 59733,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Update the first voice's timed effect. When its remaining count reaches zero, clear its active flag and envelope registers and set its completion flag. Otherwise count down the effect, periodically reload its frequency and add or subtract its configured frequency step before writing SID voice 1."
  },
  {
   "address": 59869,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Update the second voice's timed effect: clear its flag and envelope on expiry, otherwise count down, reload and step its frequency and write SID voice 2."
  },
  {
   "address": 60005,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Update the third voice's timed effect: clear its flag and envelope on expiry, otherwise count down, reload and step its frequency and write SID voice 3."
  }
 ]
}